 Let $\angle ADE = x$ degrees and $\angle DEC = 2x$ degrees.  Since triangle $AED$ is isosceles and $\angle AED = x + 70$, then \[\angle AED = \angle ADE  \Rightarrow x + 70 = x,\] a contradiction. Therefore the diagram must be rigged, with $\angle AED = \angle BED = 1 supplementary$ to each. Then $x + 70 = 90$, so $x = 20.$  From this, we see that $2x = 40.$

